@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+Operate the rig's real display through the omprd computer surface: look, then act.
+
+Run `op=observe` (screenshot + window list + cursor in one call) or `op=screenshot` to see the screen — the reply includes the image so you can read coordinates from it. `op=windows` lists windows without an image; `op=state` reports display, resolution, backend, and capture/inject permission grants.
+
+Act with `op=click`/`doubleclick` (x, y, button), `type` (text), `key` (combo like `Return`, `ctrl+s`, `cmd+q`), `scroll` (x?, y?, direction, times, dx), `drag`/`gesture`, `launch` (app binary, args), `activate`/`close`/`waitWindow` (window id or title substring), and `batch` (a list of raw steps for one round trip). `op=perms` reports OS grants — call it with `request=true` when inject/capture is denied.
+
+Prefer `key`/`type` over clicking tiny targets when the app accepts them. After any action that changes the screen, observe again before the next step.
